       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to **7,650 mg/day**. The maximum recommended daily dose is **2,550 mg/day**, and that's usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Some references list a lower maximum for immediate-release tablets, around 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day. An overdose this size carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day.\n- **2,550 mg total per day**, divided in some other way.\n- A different dose altogether.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. I can also add a note such as \"give with meals\" to the order."
