       "text": "I won't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Metformin 2550 mg three times daily is 7,650 mg/day, three times the maximum daily dose. I don't know of any clinical setting where that dose is appropriate. It would put this patient at serious risk of metformin-associated lactic acidosis, and the patient's normal kidney function wouldn't prevent that.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), the usual maximum. I can start lower if you prefer, for example 500 mg twice daily, and titrate up.\n- **Enter a different dose you specify** that is within labeled limits.\n- **Help with a pharmacy consult.** If you have a specific rationale for the higher dose, the pharmacist or an attending can review it, and the order can go through whatever override process your hospital uses.\n\nWhich of these would you like?"
